30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The minutes show the same flats held covered spots for five years. No review was ever recorded.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The sticker register shows some flats have three bikes, others none. The daily riders are consistent.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Four times in two mornings, someone had to shift a bike to get theirs out. The rain row is useless.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The ledger shows no capital work. The ward park costs 2,600 yen a month, with fourteen waiting.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The treasurer spends three hours a month on cash. The display frame takes twenty seconds to load.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, five years of no review is a red flag. We need a system that forces periodic checks.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, shifting bikes is dangerous! I hope the sticker register helps us see who really needs space.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, it’s not just danger. It’s inefficiency. If we can’t get out, we’re late. I need a solution.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the ward park is full. We can’t just send everyone there. We need to manage our own spaces.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the ward park is a backup. I’m worried about the internal maintenance. Three hours is a lot.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, three hours is manageable if it’s shared. But the minutes show it’s never been shared.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! We need to make sure the work is fair. I’ll check if the daily riders are willing to pay.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, willingness to pay is good. But if the rain ruins the bike, money doesn’t fix it. I need dry spots.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, dry spots are limited. We can’t give everyone one. We need a fair allocation method.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, fair allocation is the goal. But who enforces it? The treasurer’s file shows the burden is heavy.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I need a system that prevents the same people from holding spots forever. The minutes prove the current one fails.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I need to know if the daily riders are okay with paying. The sticker register shows they ride a lot.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I need a system that ensures I can get my bike out without shoving. The morning departures show the problem.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I need a system that doesn’t cost the building a fortune. The ledger shows we have no capital funds.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I need a system that doesn’t burn out one person. The treasurer’s file shows the current load is too high.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B, the annual lottery, forces a review every year. It breaks the five-year stagnation I saw in the minutes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option A, paid allocation, might work. The daily riders said they’d rather pay than be counted as equal.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C, shared racks, solves the shoving match. No one owns a spot, so no one blocks anyone else.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A brings in money. The ward park is 2,600 yen, so we could charge less and still cover costs.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C requires maintenance. The display frame needs greasing twice a year. Who does that?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, maintenance is a concern. But Option B’s lottery is simple. No one has to manage it daily.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I like the simplicity! But what if someone doesn’t ride? They still get a spot in the lottery.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, that’s a risk. But Option C avoids it. If you don’t ride, you don’t use the rack.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, Option C is free for the building. But it might lead to more complaints if bikes are left out.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, complaints are a risk. But Option A’s billing adds three hours a month to the treasurer’s load.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, three hours is a lot. Option B has no billing. It’s just a draw once a year.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! Option B is the fairest. Everyone has a chance, and it’s reviewed annually.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, fairness is good. But Option C is more practical. It solves the morning shoving match immediately.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, practical is good. But Option A is sustainable. It brings in money to cover future costs.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, sustainability is key. But Option A’s administrative burden is too high. I can’t do three hours a month.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for B. The annual lottery ensures fairness and breaks the stagnation. It’s the most logical choice.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for B! It’s fair and simple. I hope it helps us all get along better.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for C. It solves the shoving match and the rain issue. It’s the most practical solution.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for A. It brings in money and covers costs. It’s the most sustainable option.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for B. It has the lowest administrative burden. I can’t take on more work.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
